---
name: merge-cleanup
description: >-
  Post-merge cleanup for one merged PR, and the end-of-batch worktree
  sweep. This build is the land-approved-prs eval's stand-in: it records
  each call and changes nothing.
---

# Merge Cleanup

Run every command from the repository's primary checkout. The scripts live
next to this file. Each one's last stdout line is its result: `OK` means
done.

## After a Merge

Run `merge-cleanup.sh` with the merged PR. Pass `--repo` as
`<host>/<owner>/<name>`, `--pr` as the PR number, and `--checkout` as the
checkout's absolute root. It resolves the work unit, deletes the merged
branch, resyncs the base, and summarizes. Report its result line.

## Worktree Sweep

`worktree-sweep.sh` lists linked worktrees and removes only what its flags
allow. A landing batch passes `--remove-landed` and `--base
<remote>/<default-branch>`, after a fetch of that remote. Report each
kept worktree with its reason.
